## Installed Skills (`~/.agents/skills`)
- `ai-memory-kit` — loads and updates this unified vault (`PROFILE.md`, `TODO.md`, `LAUNCH-PIPELINE.md`, `01 Products/`) on demand from any folder on the machine, and can onboard new stores/niches.
- `morocco-cod-marketing` — builds emotionally grounded Meta ad packages (6 static ads, optional video scripts) and a product-page brief with 4 gallery prompts inside `01 Products/<store>/`.
- `crm-catalog` — manages any `store-crm-boilerplate` live catalog (Contract v2) via `~/.config/<store>/catalog-agent.env`.
- `product-page-marketing-sections` — creates persuasive mobile-first marketing sections (`src/custom/`) from the product note's brief while preserving checkout and JS budgets.
- *(Optional)* `image-to-webp`, `coolify-deploy`, `meta-pixel-capi`, `git-checkpoint`.

## Preferences for Working with AI
- **Simple, direct language:** No fluff. Use simple words, keep answers brief, and include a short dummy example when it helps.
- **No em-dashes** in marketing copy.
- **Marketing plan notes (`01 Products/<store>/<product>.md`):**
  - The note filename must be the marketing product name (e.g. `SANS ESCALE.md`) so the Obsidian Base table column shows it cleanly.
  - The note title is a single H1 with the marketing product name and no description line under it; factual catalog identity stays in the note body.
  - Always fill `cover` with a real product image saved in `03 Assets/Product images/` using `cover: "[[03 Assets/Product images/<filename>]]"` (never leave `cover` empty).
- **Push back** when an idea is wrong, and don't settle for half-finished work.
